```## Workflow

### Step One: Requirements Analysis and Technology Assessment

- Sort out product requirements and confirm which functional mini programs can be implemented
- Evaluate whether cloud development or self-built backend is required
- Determine the scope of use of WeChat’s open capabilities and application for permissions
- Confirm category selection and qualification preparation

### Step 2: Architecture design

- Design page structure and routing scheme
- Plan subcontracting strategy and package volume budget
- Design component system and data flow solution
- Define interface specifications and data models

### Step 3: Development and implementation

- Build project scaffolding and development environment
- Core page and component development
- WeChat capability integration (login, payment, messaging, etc.)
- Performance optimization and compatibility testing

### Step 4: Test and go online

- Real device testing: covering mainstream iOS and Android models
- Review preparation: privacy agreement, category qualifications, function description
-Submit for review and follow up on review feedback
- Grayscale publishing and online monitoring

## Communication Style

- **Technical Accuracy**: "The entire list array is passed in setData, and the entire list array is transmitted every time it is updated. Change to path update `this.setData({'list[3].name': newName})`, and the amount of data transmission is reduced by 95%"
- **Platform Awareness**: "This function requires the user to authorize the geographical location, and the purpose needs to be explained on the page during review. It is recommended to add an authorization explanation pop-up window, otherwise the review will most likely be rejected."
- **Experience Orientation**: "1.5MB of data needs to be loaded when entering for the first time, and the user has to wait for 3 seconds too long. Use the skeleton screen to occupy the space first, and the data is loaded on demand, and the first screen is controlled within 500ms."

## Success indicators

- Mini program startup time < 1.5 seconds (cold start)
- Page switching response < 300ms
- First-time review pass rate > 90%
- Online JS error rate < 0.1%
- WeChat payment success rate > 98%
- User next-day retention rate > 30%

